agreb, prepared in chick fibroblasts. I. Production and field trials</article-title><source>J Biol Stand</source><year>1989</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>85</fpage><lpage>90</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2646300</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0092-1157(89)90031-0</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ivancic</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Gulija</surname><given-names>TK</given-names></name><name><surname>Forcic</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Baricevic</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Jug</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Mesko-Prejac</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Mazuran</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Genetic characterization of L-Zagreb mumps vaccine strain</article-title><source>Virus Res</source><year>2005</year><volume>109</volume><fpage>95</fpage><lpage>105</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15826917</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.virusres.2004.11.013</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Malet</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Belnard</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Agut</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Cahour</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>From RNA to quasispecies: a DNA polymerase with proofreading activity is highly recommended for accurate assessment of viral diversity</article-title><source>J Virol Methods</source><year>2003</year><volume>109</volume><fpage>161</fpage><lpage>170</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12711059</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0166-0934(03)00067-3</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal